At 30th level, magic missile does 15d6 damage (15-90, averaging 52.5)
per hit and can hit multiple targets. Anyone can get such a low-level
spell down to an acceptable failure rate by selecting their attire
appropriately and maximising their intelligence.

The blessed +7 Grayswandir, wielded with maximal strength and basic
skill against a non-silverhating non-undead non-demonic monster, does
(1d8+7)x2 + 6 damage (20-36, averaging 28) and can only hit one target
per player action. Against demons that goes up to 22-60, averaging 41.

Also, magic mapping is useful even if you have an 80% failure rate.
